Done. Here's the setup:

**Production code** — replace `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow` with `Clock.UtcNow`:

```csharp
public bool IsOverdue(DateTimeOffset dueDate)
    => Clock.UtcNow > dueDate;
```

**Tests** — pin time with a disposable scope:

```csharp
[Fact]
public void IsOverdue_WhenPastDue_ReturnsTrue()
{
    var now = new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 9, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);
    using var _ = Clock.Override(now);

    var calc = new InvoiceCalculator();
    Assert.True(calc.IsOverdue(now.AddDays(-1)));
}
```

**Why this works well for a library with no DI:**

| Concern | Answer |
|---------|--------|
| Parallel tests | `AsyncLocal<T>` isolates each test's flow |
| Production cost | One null-check per call |
| No DI needed | Static access, no constructors change |
| Cleanup | `Dispose()` restores real time |

For any other class reading `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow`, just swap it to `Clock.UtcNow` — no constructor changes required.
